"""Case library: real climate and transition events, what they did to company assets and financials, and how companies and
institutions responded. Every fact is a sentence taken from a named source; nothing is filled in from memory.

Card fields
  id, title, year, region, kind (physical_acute | physical_chronic | transition_policy | transition_market | litigation | market_context),
  driver, assets (what was exposed), channels (how the hazard reached the financials), facts, responses, gaps, lessons.

  facts      [(text, source_index)]     the only place numbers live
  responses  [(type, text, source_index)]  type in: transfer, operational, financial, strategic, policy, disclosure
  gaps       things the sources did NOT report (the model must say "not covered" for these)
  lessons    analyst-written patterns (marked as analysis when rendered; no numbers)
  sources    [(url, outlet, tier)]  tier: "read" = the primary document was fetched and read in full,
                                            "reported" = taken from the named outlet's reporting (the verifier upgrades it when the figures are found on the page)

Channels (the reasoning frame the model is trained to use):
  asset_damage, business_interruption, supply_chain, input_shortage (power, water, transport, feedstock), liability,
  regulation_policy, market_price, financing_liquidity, insurance_availability, sovereign_backstop, demand_shift
"""

